; A SUM crossing an `if` — the dynamic tag, which is where the commuting
; expect: 0 2 4 6 10 16 1013 1021 1034
; conversion earns its place. A tag known at compile time reduces away by β
; alone; one decided at runtime gets stuck as `((if c A B) F G)` until an
; eliminator is pushed into both branches (sums.md).
;
; Neither a tag nor a closure nor an allocation should survive to any backend.
;
; The err branch adds rather than negating, and that is not arbitrary: printing
; a NEGATIVE number is outside `win/fmt.print-int`s declared domain, and the
; first version of this case found that the domain is not enforced — see
; differential-2026-08-26 §4.
(sum result (ok int) (err int))

(def step (fn (n)
  (if (>= n 10) (err n) (ok (* n 2)))))

(def run (fn (n)
  (case (step n)
    (ok v)  v
    (err e) (+ e 1000))))
